---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/07-10/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/07-10/interactions.json';
import {vertices,sides} from '../../../../lib/equipment/07-10/solver.mjs';
const a='/equipment/07-10/',photo='https://www.rockefeller.edu/fcrc/uploads/www.rockefeller.edu/sites/147/2017/02/BD_FACSAria_II_cell_sorter_brochure-23-9640-00.pdf#page=1',spec='https://www.bdbiosciences.com/content/dam/bdb/marketing-documents/BD_FACSAria_II_User_Guide.pdf';
const display=x=>typeof x==='string'?x:Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+String(v)).join('; ');
const X=x=>148+17*x,Y=y=>149-17*y;
---
<Layout pageTitle="BD FACSAria II documentary view" subtitle="" description="Inspect a sealed FACSAria II model and read the lengths of an independent abstract triangle." wide={true}>
<article id="aria" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/07-10/">← Equipment 07-10</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#aria-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">07-10 / BD FACSAria II / Sealed documentary shell</p><h2>BD FACSAria II</h2><p>Inspect the sealed, unpowered exterior. On a detached desk, use three fixed drawing points to read the sides of a 6–8–10 triangle. The diagram never interacts with the instrument.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the static cabinet</h3><div id="aria-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Exterior','Desk'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="aria-xr" type="button" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div><canvas id="aria-model" aria-label="Orbitable sealed FACSAria II exterior and separate triangle desk"></canvas><p id="aria-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">Only the desk keys and monitor respond. The cabinet and front remain opaque and fixed. Drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Choose a fixed side</h3><div class="e-fields"><label>Drawing side<select id="aria-side">{Object.keys(sides).map(k=><option value={k} selected={k==='CA'}>{k}</option>)}</select></label></div><div class="e-row"><button id="aria-reset" type="button">Restore diagonal</button><button id="aria-json" class="e-run" disabled>Export side JSON</button></div><p id="aria-status" role="status">No diagram read.</p><p id="aria-result" role="status">No length read.</p></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Read the fixed triangle</h3><svg id="aria-diagram" viewBox="0 0 350 241" role="img" aria-label="Fixed abstract triangle with three selectable sides"><path d="M48 149H288M148 56V204" stroke="#a2b3af" fill="none"/>{Object.entries(sides).map(([k,[p,q]])=><line data-side={k} class={k==='CA'?'selected':''} x1={X(vertices[p][0])} y1={Y(vertices[p][1])} x2={X(vertices[q][0])} y2={Y(vertices[q][1])}/>)}{Object.entries(vertices).map(([k,[x,y]])=><g><circle cx={X(x)} cy={Y(y)} r="4.5" fill="#335564"/><text x={X(x)+8} y={Y(y)-8} fill="#335564" font-size="13">{k} ({x}, {y})</text></g>)}<text x="45" y="226" font-size="13" fill="#294c5c">Original triangle · abstract drawing units</text></svg>
<p>The points are immutable. The readout uses √(ΔX² + ΔY²); it never accepts external points or filters a dataset. JSON stores the source ID, endpoints, signed differences and length. <a href={a+'example-side.json'}>Example JSON</a>.</p></section>
<section><h3>Documentary geometry</h3><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original dark blue and silver BD exterior with detached triangle desk"/><figcaption>Original shape from <a href={photo}>BD’s cover photograph</a>. The desks and display are original scene props.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original sealed two-tone BD FACSAria II outer cabinet"/><figcaption>Opaque front surfaces are modeled in place of visible internal areas. No compartments can open.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Quantity</th><th>Reference</th><th>Parsed GLB</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Width × depth × height</td><td><a href={spec}>BD guide, table 8-1, p. 248</a>: 1,220 × 710 × 710 mm</td><td>1,220 × 710 × 710 mm. Numerical scene check, not a physical measurement.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>Cabinet trim and covers are original estimates. No assays, sorting, gating, sampling, biological handling, functioning controls, instrument settings, or laser are modeled. The register’s population acceptance is excluded.</p></section>
<section id="aria-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{display(x.expected)}</td><td>{display(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'bd-facsaria-ii.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Named targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles and {m.draws} draw primitives; optional WebXR, physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/07-10/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#aria header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#aria h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#aria section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#aria button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#aria button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#aria-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#aria-chart{width:100%;max-height:16rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#aria table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#aria td,#aria th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#aria figure{margin:0}#aria img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
#aria caption{text-align:left}#aria input,#aria select,#aria button{min-width:0}#aria .e-hint{font-size:.92rem}#aria-diagram{display:block;width:min(100%,36rem);height:auto;background:#edeae0}#aria-diagram [data-side]{cursor:pointer;stroke:#61778e;stroke-width:3}#aria-diagram .selected{stroke:#c78039;stroke-width:5}</style>
